# Architecture & folder structure

## Target layout (Next.js App Router)

```
app/                          # Routes only — thin page shells
  (routes)/page.tsx
  api/<resource>/route.ts     # Thin handlers — delegate to lib/
components/
  atoms/                      # Button, Input, Icon, Label
  molecules/                  # SearchBar, FormField, Card
  organisms/                  # Header, GlossaryTable, TranslatorPanel
  pages/                      # Page-level compositions (optional; or keep in app/)
hooks/                        # useGlossary, useTranslation — stateful UI logic
lib/                          # Pure business logic, parsers, validators
services/                     # External API clients (Anthropic, etc.)
types/                        # Shared TypeScript interfaces
tests/                        # Unit + integration tests (mirrors source layout)
  lib/                        # tests/lib/bereken-niveau.test.ts → lib/bereken-niveau.ts
  hooks/
  services/
  app/api/
  helpers/                    # Shared test utilities (auth mocks, fixtures)
  setup.ts                    # Vitest global setup
```

## Atomic design rules

- **atoms** — zero business logic; props in, JSX out
- **molecules** — compose atoms; may use local UI state only
- **organisms** — compose molecules; receive data + callbacks via props
- **pages / app routes** — wire organisms to hooks/services; no inline business logic

## Separate UI from logic

| Layer | Responsibility | Example |
|-------|----------------|---------|
| `components/` | Presentation | `<GlossaryRow term={t} onSave={fn} />` |
| `hooks/` | Stateful orchestration | `useGlossary()` — fetch, mutate, loading |
| `lib/` | Pure functions | `parseXliff()`, `validateTerm()` |
| `services/` | I/O boundaries | `translateBatch()`, `sql` queries |
| `app/api/` | Auth + HTTP + delegate | `auth()` → `lib/glossary.ts` |

❌ Business logic in JSX event handlers beyond trivial glue  
❌ Direct `fetch` to external APIs from components — use `services/` or server actions  
✅ Custom hooks encapsulate data fetching and mutations  
✅ `lib/` functions are testable without React

## File size limit

**Maximum 300 lines per file** (excluding generated files and lockfiles).

When a file approaches 250 lines, split proactively:
- Extract helpers to `lib/`
- Extract sub-components to the next atomic level
- Extract hook logic to `hooks/`

## Imports

- Use `@/` path alias for project root
- Components import down the atomic hierarchy only (organism → molecule → atom)
- `lib/` and `services/` must not import from `components/`
